# red7: a bare H1-vs-H2 byte comparison fails on framing, proving only
# de-framed guest bytes can be the invariant.
#
# The first form of `production_serve_h1_h2_event_bytes_identical` compared
# the H1 body (with chunk framing) directly against the de-framed H2 answer
# on the live-probe SSE fixture (`sse-event.wat`, `data: hello` events).
# It failed as it must: the left side is three bare `data: hello` events
# (de-framed H2 DATA payloads); the right side interleaves each event with
# its `d\r\n...\r\n` chunk envelope. Same guest bytes, different wire
# framing — which is why the committed test de-chunks H1 first and compares
# event bytes only. A "byte-identical H1 answer" claim at the wire level
# would be false for every HTTP version pair; at the guest-event level it
# holds and this test pins it.
#
# Captured from a real run against the echo fixture, then the test was
# fixed (dechunk_prefix + whole-event read) and re-ran green.

